// Native-scatter schedule — single worker, no decomposition.
//
// Drives `prog.scatter.algo.nuc` (the native data-dependent WRITE
// histogram, TASK-0376) rather than the masked `prog.algo.nuc`. The e2e
// harness selects the algorithm from this `schedule for` path
// (TASK-0049.03 per-cell algo selection) and pairs `kernels.scatter.rs`
// by the variant rule (TASK-0049.08), so an `08-histogram/scatter` cell
// compiles the scatter variant while `08-histogram/naive` keeps the
// masked form.
//
// Single worker (`host`): the data-dependent WRITE `histogram[input[i]]`
// needs the whole of `histogram` mutable on one worker, which the
// single-worker placement trivially satisfies (no transfers, no
// cross-worker bin fan-in). The DISTRIBUTED scatter (partition the
// input, per-worker partial histograms, cross-worker element-wise-sum
// combine) is the sibling `distributed.scatter.sched.nuc` (TASK-0384);
// it is NOT exercised by THIS single-worker schedule. Output is
// bit-identical to 08-histogram/naive and reference.bin.

schedule for "../prog.scatter.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input  on host;
    place save_output on host;
    place inc         on host;

    // No loop transforms, no transfer directives (single worker).
}
